<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea buys 40,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 soybean.</title>
<headline>S.Korea buys 40,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's state Agricultural and Fishery Marketing Corp (AFMC) on Tuesday bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. No 1 soybean from Louis Dreyfus and another 20,000 tonnes from Continental Grain, an official at the corporation said.  </p>
<p>Arrival of the first 20,000 tonnes is set for September 20 and the remaining 20,000 tonnes for October 20, both to the western port of Inchon, he said.</p>
<p>Details of the purchase are as follows:</p>
<p> POSITION TONNE	   SHIPMENT		     PRICE</p>
<p>			 U.S. Gulf	U.S. PNW	(per tonne)</p>
<p>   ONE    20,000  Jul 26-Aug 15  Aug 11-30     $304.08/FOB</p>
<p>   TWO    20,000  Aug 26-Sep 15  Sep 11-30     $326.54/C&amp;F</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
